✅ DRUV AI — PREFLIGHT CHECKLIST (MANDATORY BEFORE ANY CHANGE)

Cursor MUST run this checklist mentally and explicitly before touching code.
If any item fails → STOP.

🧠 1. CONTEXT & INTENT CHECK

Before writing code, answer all:

 What exact problem am I solving?

 Which existing file/module already handles this?

 Is this a bug fix, behavior change, or activation of existing intelligence?

 Am I modifying behavior or just improving quality?

🚫 If intent is unclear → STOP and ask.

🔍 2. SEARCH BEFORE WRITE (ZERO DUPLICATION)

Cursor must confirm:

 I searched the codebase for similar logic

 I identified the single source of truth

 I am NOT creating:

new agent

new orchestrator

new router

new memory layer

new “v2 / enhanced / alternate” file

✅ Allowed: modify existing logic in-place

🚫 If similar logic already exists → reuse it.

🧱 3. WORKING FLOW PROTECTION

Cursor must verify:

 Existing APIs will still work

 Existing routes/endpoints are untouched

 Existing UI behavior is not broken

 No public interface is renamed

 No working logic is removed

Rule:

If it works today, it must work tomorrow.

🧠 4. AGENTIC INTEGRITY CHECK

If touching anything called an agent:

 Does it have reasoning (loop or planning)?

 Does it use tools OR consciously avoid them?

 Does it use memory/state where applicable?

 Is it triggered dynamically (not hardcoded)?

🚫 If NO → treat it as a response layer, not an agent
🚫 Do NOT fake agent behavior with prompts

🚫 5. NO HARDCODED INTELLIGENCE

Strictly confirm:

 No keyword-based responses added

 No string-specific hacks (“need support”, “great”, etc.)

 No fixed templates pretending to be reasoning

✅ Allowed:

Semantic classifier

LLM-based decision

Confidence-based routing

🔁 6. NO PARTIAL CHANGES

Cursor must confirm:

 The change is complete end-to-end

 Routing → Agent → Response → Fallback are all handled

 No TODOs left behind

 No “we’ll handle later”

🚫 Partial work is NOT allowed in this system.

👁️ 7. OBSERVABILITY CHECK

For any behavioral change:

 request_id is preserved

 routing decision is logged

 agent activation is logged

 tool usage is logged (if any)

 failures have explicit logs

If you can’t observe it → it doesn’t exist.

🛑 PREFLIGHT FAIL RULE

If any single checkbox fails:

❌ DO NOT WRITE CODE
📣 Explain findings + ask for direction

🔐 DRUV AI — AI SAFETY GATE (PR / CHANGE APPROVAL)

This gate decides whether a change is ALLOWED, BLOCKED, or REQUIRES REVIEW

🟢 GATE 1: DUPLICATION SAFETY

BLOCK if ANY are true:

New file added when similar file exists

New agent created instead of activating existing one

Parallel orchestrator / router introduced

Same logic implemented in multiple places

➡️ Result: ❌ BLOCK

🟡 GATE 2: AGENTIC TRUTH CHECK

Ask:

Is this change making the system actually think more?

Or just sound smarter?

BLOCK if:

Prompt-only intelligence added

Persona expanded without reasoning

Tools mentioned but not invoked

Memory claimed but not used

➡️ Result: ❌ BLOCK

🟢 GATE 3: ROUTING & FREEDOM CHECK

Ensure:

 No student input category is blocked

 Casual / emotional / vague queries still respond

 Off-topic queries are redirected, not rejected

 No over-restrictive patterns added

If any input becomes unreachable → BLOCK

🟡 GATE 4: REGRESSION SAFETY

Verify:

Existing tests still pass (if present)

No duplicate responses introduced

No silent behavior changes

No UI regressions

If uncertain → ⚠️ REQUIRE REVIEW

🔴 GATE 5: CONFIDENCE RULE

Cursor must explicitly state:

“I am confident this change does not duplicate logic, break flows, or fake intelligence.”

If Cursor cannot confidently say this:

➡️ ❌ BLOCK

🧠 FINAL SAFETY PRINCIPLE (THIS IS LAW)

Druv AI must never get smarter by hacks.
It must get smarter by thinking more often.

Default to ReAct

Default to reasoning

Default to reuse

Default to safety

Default to restraint